# Per-machine direnv environment for this repo's spec pipeline (spec 025).
#
# ONE-TIME SETUP:
#   1. Install direnv (https://direnv.net) and wire the hook once in your
#      shell profile:
#        eval "$(direnv hook bash)"   # or your shell's hook
#   2. Copy this template to the repo root and allow it:
#        cp templates/.envrc.example .envrc
#        direnv allow
#      The repo-root .envrc is PER-MACHINE and gitignored — NEVER commit it.
#
# WHAT EACH LINE LOADS (later lines win: a dotenv line clobbers any
# pre-existing value, exported shell vars included — the .envrc is the
# per-directory source of truth):
#   1. config/model.local.env.example — committed defaults for the 8
#      SPEC_*_MODEL vars opencode.json interpolates. Loaded first so every var
#      is non-empty when opencode launches ({env:VAR} resolves empty when
#      unset — this opencode build has no default syntax).
#   2. config/model.local.env — gitignored per-machine override.
#   3. config/agent.local.env — gitignored per-machine credentials
#      (GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN).
dotenv_if_exists config/model.local.env.example
dotenv_if_exists config/model.local.env
dotenv_if_exists config/agent.local.env
